course: dictionary
lesson: 1780
title: Climb: up, up and up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word climb has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. To climb is to go up something, like stairs, a tree, a ladder or a mountain, often using your hands and feet. «Most stories climb a story mountain» means the story goes up in steps, like a path up a hill.
explain: To climb can also mean to go up in amount. Prices climbing means prices are getting higher, and temperatures climbing means it is getting warmer. A climb can be a noun too: a trip up a hill is a climb, and so is a hard way up.
explain: Ask yourself: is something going up a height, or is a number going higher? Then put your meaning into the sentence. «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window» only makes sense if climb means move up and in with your body, which is why it is unsafe.
fact: Climb means to go up something, often using your hands and feet.
fact: Climb can also mean to go up in amount, like prices or temperatures.
fact: A climb is a trip up, or a hard way up.
fact: «Never climb on or hang from a soccer goal; unanchored goals can fall and crush children.» If a goal wobbles, tell an adult.
fact: Climb is a verb, and its other forms are climbs, climbed and climbing. A climb is also a noun.
exercise: «Think of a parrot climbing its cage: beak, foot, beak, foot.» What is the parrot doing? | *Going up its cage, using its beak and feet | Flying out of the window | Singing a song | Sleeping in a box
exercise: «Prices climb every winter.» What does climb mean here? | Hold on to a rope | Stop moving | *Go up in amount | Go down a hill
exercise: «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window.» What should you do instead? | Wait on the roof | Break the window with a stone | *Call a parent or go to a trusted neighbour | Climb in quickly before anyone sees
test: «The hikers made a steep climb up the mountain.» In this sentence, climb is a | adverb | *noun | verb | adjective
test: «Ben climbed the tree while Sam watched from below.» Find and copy the word that is a form of climb. | below | tree | watched | *climbed
exam: In «A snail climbs up a well by day and slides back at night», what does climbs mean? | Goes round | Stops | Goes down | *Goes up
